{"title":"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the first term of an infinite geometric series is a positive integer, the common ratio is the reciprocal of a positive integer, and the sum of the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the sum of the first two terms of the series is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f9b4c1bbac17af44db9f0be9c165ca64273dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{8}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2           \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{9}{2} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"363\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the first term and common ratio of the series, respectively.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a70212649703c60ad6bc13d9a31a4086ba68b2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f221038bf084ac23568cbf2af37d570107558547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{1-r} = \\frac{a}{1-\\frac{1}{b}} = \\frac{ab}{b-1} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"217\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f38aa98532de09f1fdabfc1cff89a096cdc8fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = 3(b-1) = 3b - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362f24c016c90d86f36989590270ebb5fadcc53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab - 3b = b(a-3) = -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36ddba89eb5035af6d0d797c475171b9df6c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> are both integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.  But if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> which is not positive.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/55460c108a253af8eb0a5dc16f7d460d52f6a5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />.  So the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms of the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e652404bcd67695e6f3198b9d8a4b96421e811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + \\frac{2}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{8}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"129\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~PhysicsDolphin, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1975 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"197